---
// FAQ Section
---

<section id="faq" class="faq section">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

    <div class="faq-grid">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Is FollowBirds only for Algarve?</h3>
        <p>
          FollowBirds is starting in Algarve, Portugal. The goal is to become excellent locally before expanding to other regions.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Can guides use it for tours?</h3>
        <p>
          Yes. FollowBirds is being designed around guide workflows: tour templates, shared observations, live checklists and automatic reports.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Can birdwatchers use it without joining a tour?</h3>
        <p>
          Yes. Birdwatchers can explore birds, locations and checklists independently.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Does it work offline?</h3>
        <p>
          The app is offline-first. Bird and location content should remain useful even without connection.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Are reports automatic?</h3>
        <p>
          The planned report system generates web/PDF reports from tour observations, species lists, photos, notes and route information. Reports are generated after each tour.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Is the guide program available now?</h3>
        <p>
          The guide program is intended for early professional guides in Algarve. Join the program to get listed early and help shape the tools.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>What about birdwatcher pricing?</h3>
        <p>
          Birdwatchers can explore birds, locations and checklists independently. As we develop the platform, pricing for advanced features will remain transparent and fair.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>How do I share tour reports?</h3>
        <p>
          After a tour, FollowBirds generates a shareable web link for the report. Participants can view and download PDF reports at any time.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq {
    background-color: #FFFFFF;
  }

  .faq h2 {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .faq-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(350px, 1fr));
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .faq-item {
    padding: 2.25rem;
    background: #FAF7EF;
    border-radius: 0.85rem;
    border: 1px solid #E8DFD3;
    transition: all 0.3s ease;
  }

  .faq-item:hover {
    border-color: #2F7D32;
    box-shadow: 0 6px 16px rgba(47, 125, 50, 0.08);
  }

  .faq-item h3 {
    color: #2F7D32;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .faq-item p {
    color: #5E6B60;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .faq-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
